  "summary_en": "Latvian translation of the 2017 UNESCO COMEST report on robotics ethics. It surveys robot definitions, AI, and applications across industry, military, transport, health, education, home and agriculture, discusses responsibility, agency and moral status, and recommends ethical codes, value-sensitive design, meaningful human control of weapons, drone licensing and impact assessments.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Distinguishes deterministic from cognitive robots, with differing responsibility and regulation (legal vs codes and ethics guidelines).",
   "Recommends ethical codes for roboticists and integrating ethics into engineering curricula and value-sensitive design.",
   "Recommends maintaining meaningful human control over weapons and force; autonomous weapons should not be used in policing.",
   "Recommends licensing and strict limits on private drones, public policy and audit for police drones, and banning weaponised domestic drones.",
   "Calls for workforce retraining, life-cycle environmental assessment and small-scale experimentation before deployment."
